143:Figures S2 and S5 quantify the spatial overlap across scales for the HCtest cohort for negative and positive extreme deviations, respectively. Because there were fewer signi /uniFB01 cant case-control differences in overlap for positive deviations (Figures S5 -S9), we focused on negative WMV deviations (i.e., areas where volume is lower than normative expectations). We quanti /uniFB01 ed heterogeneity in WMV deviations as the proportion of individuals showing an extreme deviation in each voxel, estimated separately for each diagnostic group and the HCtest cohort. Across all groups, we found very little spatial overlap in the location of voxel-scale negative extreme deviations, with the maximum percentage overlap never exceeding 5% (Table 2 and Figure 1F, G).


